{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The kindnesses of YHWH forever I will sing</b> — If this is Eitan, he is the one mentioned who is a son of Zerah, concerning whom Scripture says 'Eitan the Ezrachite' (1 Kings 5:11) — he prophesied concerning the kingdom of David, that it would be cut off. Now there was in Spain a great and pious sage, and this psalm was difficult for him, and he would not read it nor could he bear to hear it, because this poet speaks harshly against the honored Name. And the Gaon [Saadia] did not explicitly mention a correction for this psalm. And R. Moses ha-Kohen lengthened on this matter, and I examined his book several times and could not understand his words. Now the secret of this psalm: as it begins 'The kindnesses of YHWH' — he recounts the kindnesses of HaShem and what He swore to David, and he speaks concerning the words of the enemies, who revile and deny. Therefore he mentions 'the reproach of Your servants, which Your enemies have reproached, O YHWH' (v. 51), and the conclusion of his words indicates that he believes in the coming of the Messiah — 'they have reproached the footsteps of Your anointed' (v. 51) — as I shall explain." "<b>The kindnesses of</b> — the Name, and His faithfulness, forever. Rich."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {0 "Resolution of בן זרח/מאיתן האזרחי based on 1 Kings 5:11 genealogy; 'תיקון' rendered as 'correction' following the Gaon's editorial term for problematic biblical readings."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:28.737505755Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}